  "answer": "Nothing is broken, and the claims should not be deleted or recreated.\n\nThe namespace sandbox-r7tbm-rhel-ha-cluster-lab is on cluster ocpv-cobalt. It has 3 PVCs, all Pending: rhel-ha-node1-rootdisk, rhel-ha-node2-rootdisk and rhel-ha-node3-rootdisk (40Gi each, Block, storage class lvms-nvme-thin). Each one carries the same event: \"WaitForFirstConsumer: waiting for first consumer to be created before binding\".\n\nThat is how their storage class is meant to behave. lvms-nvme-thin (provisioner topolvm.io, the cluster default) has binding_mode WaitForFirstConsumer. LVM storage is local to a node, so a claim is not bound until a pod or VM that uses it is scheduled. Only then does the volume get carved out on that VM's node.\n\nNothing is using them yet. The 3 VMs, rhel-ha-node1, rhel-ha-node2 and rhel-ha-node3, are all Stopped, with condition VMINotExists (\"VMI does not exist\"). They were created stopped for tomorrow's session, so there is no first consumer. When the VMs are started at 09:00, each claim binds on the node its VM lands on.\n\nThe Pending state is expected and needs no action. Deleting and recreating the claims would change nothing: they would come back Pending, for the same reason, until the VMs start. If a claim is still Pending after its VM has been started, that would be worth investigating.\n"
